{"base_rate":0.38110236220472443,"brier":0.18322929133858265,"bss":0.22315489033289182,"bss_hi":0.3146844278891172,"bss_lo":0.1299584734890858,"chart":{"base":[556.2,65.4],"fp":[312.7,324.3],"note":{"base":"skill 0.22 — higher than 32% of cities","fp":"low end +11pp, high end +10pp","rel":"promised 0% → rained 5%; promised 89% → rained 72%"},"rel":"62,442.4 80.5,402.5 149.7,337.8 346.4,187.8 622.1,154.6"},"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.14062992125984253,"ess":472.0316582736761,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Toronto</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Toronto rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (97%), believe about\n<b>77%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 635 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-20. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nTORONTO 9.7 ENE, 10.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.22, ranked 145 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(94&ndash;167) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>110</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>62</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'><b>39%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>57%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>80%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>63</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>77%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Toronto</b> <span class=\"muted\">Canada</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.22</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>94&ndash;167\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>635 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Toronto &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Toronto\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=