"311.5483870967742\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 18%&amp;#10;It rained 39% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"122.04181818181819\" cy=\"238.60606060606062\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 68 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"177.89147058823534\" cy=\"194.64705882352942\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 57%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"260.2225\" cy=\"97.625\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 80%&amp;#10;It rained 67% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 63 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"341.4809523809524\" cy=\"139.33333333333334\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 77% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 66 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"402.56000000000006\" cy=\"100.72727272727275\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(38%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Toronto the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (0.10).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>169</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.098</td><td class='num'>15.2%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>164</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.119</td><td class='num'>16.0%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>136</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.163</td><td class='num'>13.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>166</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.483</td><td class='num'>9.3%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.70643,"lon":-79.39864,"n":635,"n_cities":213,"name":"Toronto","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":110,"obs":0.05454545454545454,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.014264705882352943,"n":68,"obs":0.20588235294117646,"sig":true},{"hi":0.07,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.044411764705882345,"n":68,"obs":0.08823529411764706,"sig":false},{"hi":0.14,"lo":0.07,"mean":0.09467741935483873,"n":62,"obs":0.1935483870967742,"sig":true},{"hi":0.26,"lo":0.14,"mean":0.1809090909090909,"n":66,"obs":0.3939393939393939,"sig":true},{"hi":0.45,"lo":0.26,"mean":0.33867647058823536,"n":68,"obs":0.5147058823529411,"sig":true},{"hi":0.68,"lo":0.45,"mean":0.57125,"n":64,"obs":0.78125,"sig":true},{"hi":0.91,"lo":0.68,"mean":0.8007936507936508,"n":63,"obs":0.6666666666666666,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.91,"mean":0.9733333333333335,"n":66,"obs":0.7727272727272727,"sig":true}],"